    "description": "Some items have chips as shown.\nTitle\n: Lot Of 12 Pcs Glass Insulators Telephone Telegraph Pole Antique Mixed Condition\nBrand\n: Hemingray\nColor\n: Clear and aqua\nMaterial\n: Glass\nType\n: Telephone/telegraph pole insulator\nCategory\n: Antiques\nDepartment\n: Antiques\nCategoryselection\n: Collectibles & Art\nCondition\n: Fair - shows sign of wear\nApproximate measurements (inches)\n: 13L x 13W x 9H\nWeight (approximate)\n: 13.7 lbs\nDescription\n: Add nostalgic charm to your home or collection with this lot of 12 vintage clear and aqua glass telephone and telegraph pole insulators. Each insulator features classic, heavy glass construction with varying shapes and minor variances in tint, including both clear and light aqua hues. Some show the 'HEMINGRAY' marking, a historic name in utility glassware, and all were once used to protect telecommunication wires on poles. These collectible insulators are notable for their durability, unique industrial style, and historical significance. They make excellent display decor, paperweights, or conversation pieces for vintage enthusiasts. Condition varies: some are lightly chipped, and several bear surface grime, scratches, and worn edges appropriate for items of this age. No cracks or severe breaks observed. Sold as shownplease review all photos for closer details on condition and variety. Perfect for collectors, upcycling projects, or decorative use, these insulators offer an authentic piece of telecommunications history\nCollection Of Vintage Clear Glass Telephone And Telegraph Pole Insulators",
